{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288843-2e-where-are-the-stats-for-cancer","id":1288843,"title":"(2e) Where are the stats for cancer?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-16T21:53:23-08:00","id":1288843,"title":"(2e) Where are the stats for cancer?","content":"So I went looking in 2e's corebook for the stats for cancer, since it became relevant to something I was doing in the system, but it looks like the corebook doesn't mention cancer. Anyone know if it has an untreated morbidity listed somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T22:19:22-08:00","id":1288846,"title":"","content":"Cancer, in general, can be highly variable, with some being relatively slow acting and some progressing rapidly with no hope of treatment. Given the state of medicine in the Second Age, something closer to the former is likely going to still have a high Morbidity and Treatment Difficulty, with few avenues of treatment to boot, while something closer to the latter will probably have a Morbidity and Treatment Difficulty that demand fullly-charged Excellencies from a maxed-out pool and products of powerful medicinal alchemy just to have a fighting chance without other, more sophisticated Charms.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Morbidity is probably 4-10, Treatment Difficulty as well. Untreated Morbidity is going to be higher, or potentially result in auto-failure without Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"typ